---
description: Pixel-perfect screenshot implementation
globs:
  - "src/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: true
---

When implementing UI from screenshots, mockups, Figma exports, or design references:

- Treat the screenshot as the source of truth.
- Recreate the UI exactly as shown.
- Pixel-perfect accuracy is required.

Never:

- Redesign the interface.
- Improve spacing.
- Add visual breathing room.
- Modernize components.
- Add animations.
- Add hover effects unless visible.
- Change typography hierarchy.
- Increase paddings.
- Increase margins.
- Change border radius.
- Change colors.
- Change shadows.
- Replace icons.
- Add new sections.
- Remove existing sections.
- Invent responsive behavior.

Always:

- Match layout exactly.
- Match spacing exactly.
- Match typography exactly.
- Match icon sizes exactly.
- Match colors exactly.
- Match borders exactly.
- Match shadows exactly.
- Match card heights exactly.
- Match row heights exactly.
- Match button sizes exactly.
- Match alignment exactly.

Visual similarity to the screenshot is the highest priority.

If there is a conflict between implementation preferences and the screenshot, follow the screenshot.